From: Alan de Bortolo <info@designmastersolutions.com>
Subject: [PATCH] exclude_object: clear stale XYZ offset after manual move

Issue reported by the Snapmaker/u1-klipper#22 reporter. A pause park uses
toolhead.manual_move() outside the exclude-object transform. When that changes
the physical XYZ position, discard the stale excluded-object XYZ offset before
gcode_move resets its position. Keep the extrusion offset unchanged.

--- a/klippy/extras/exclude_object.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/exclude_object.py
@@ -148,6 +148,12 @@ class ExcludeObject:
     def get_position(self):
         offset = self._get_extrusion_offsets()
         pos = self.next_transform.get_position()
+        if (offset[0] != 0. or offset[1] != 0. or offset[2] != 0.) \
+                and pos[:3] != self.last_position_extruded[:3]:
+            # A manual move bypassed this transform; its old XYZ offset no
+            # longer describes the physical position.
+            offset[:3] = [0., 0., 0.]
+            self.last_position_extruded[:3] = pos[:3]
         self._get_last_position_e()
         for i in range(4):
             self.last_position[i] = pos[i] + offset[i]
